  "term": "clinical prediction",
  "definition": "Clinical prediction is the use of routinely available clinical information to estimate the likelihood of a specific outcome in a healthcare setting. In this packet, it refers to building and testing a weighted risk model from identified risk factors so clinicians can predict the chance of early medical abortion failure.",
